Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.599 --> 00:00:03.750 align:start position:0%
 
she told many stories  but her colleagues say a lot more are  now left untold  ones only shirina boracle could so  brilliantly tell  highly regarded in palestine as a  passionate active and courageous  journalist she was devoted to telling  the palestinian story  as well as covering wars and conflicts  the veteran al jazeera journalists  reported on the smallest details of  palestinians lives conveying the harsh  realities of life under israeli military  occupation  but she too became a victim of israeli  forces when she was shot and killed  while reporting from janine in the  occupied west bank the place where  sharing was shot has turned into a  shrine where people come to pay tribute  to her  among them is iman frihat she tells us  she met the reporter in 2002 and says  shireen helped her find out her children  were alive  they told me my house was destroyed and  i thought my sons were killed under the  rubble i thought i lost them but shireen  found out they were arrested how would i  not grieve her  palestinians continue honoring shireen  who they called the daughter of  palestine paintings and murals of her  are ways some people use to keep her  legacy alive  a street in the heart of ramallah where  al jazeera's offices are based now  carries her name  sheen would pay attention to everyone  whether she meets a child or an old lady  she would sit with them for as long as  it takes to understand their story and  grievances  still she has authority while  interviewing politicians she was never  biased to any political party  all of this alongside her professional  integrity made her an icon  her colleagues remember a humble and  kind woman they worked with for more  than two decades  they say they miss working with her  especially when they covered the latest  israeli war on the besieged gaza strip  earlier this month  bashir salame added the last report  shirin worked on before she was killed  now he's editing reports on her legacy  it is tough to continue working there's  a conflict inside of me  at the same time i know that we have to  keep carrying the mantle and raising her  voice  the voice the forcibly wanted to silence  this is our motivation to keep going  many here say it's important to keep  talking about children  not only because she made palestinians  feel heard and seen but also because by  demanding justice for shireen they're  demanding justice for all the people she  reported on in her long and rich career  nida ibrahim al-jazeera the occupied  west bank  well shireen's niece lina about joins us  now from san francisco lena it's really  good to see you it's been 100 days since  your aunt's murder  we talked there about her professional  life and her legacy but 100 days on on a  personal level how are you feeling how  how is the family marking the day  thank you for having me  you know it's been 100 days and i still  wake up and ask myself if i'm in a  nightmare if this is real  100 days have been very difficult for me  and my family  trying to comprehend this insurmountable  loss  but  we continue to fight for justice  continue to fight for accountability  um and trying to keep shileen's legacy  and her memory alive  because by honoring her legacy it means  ensuring that no other journalist no  other palestinian lives  are lost and killed by the israeli  nation forces  and most importantly no other family  should have to endure what our family  has been going through for the past 100  years  that's why we continue to call for  accountability and continue our fights  for justice for shooting  talk us through how that that fight for  justice has been what does full  accountability mean for you  accountability for me and my family is  holding the soldier who killed chilean  responsible holding the entire system  that continues to perpetuate this kind  of  violence and  the chain of command that ordered the  killing of shirin  we are pursuing justice and  accountability through any means  available for us  and uh we have been encouraged by the  support of the  80 members of congress  uh that we  that we received that we saw their  efforts in calling for a u.s  investigation into the murder of the u.s  citizens  uh including um  representative andre carson's the  justice for shilling act and senator van  hollen's efforts in the senate all of  these have given us  some hope  that there will be justice for chilean  no matter what the  no matter how the road is we will not  relent we will continue to push for  accountability i remember when you were  at capitol hill and speaking with some  of those members of congress one of them  said you know if this was anywhere else  in the world  the soldier and the person who ordered  that soldier would be held accountable  but because they are in israeli  uniforms they will not be held  accountable  i mean what does that say to you do you  think that is true do you feel like  there will be some accountability as you  go down this road  of course that statement is true because  because shireen  shireen was is a palestinian-american  so the fact that there is palestinian  before american  has made the entire  uh  entire road towards accountability even  more difficult if shireen was killed  somewhere else there would have been an  investigation from day one there would  have been justice from day one but the  double standards is stark especially  that the u.s continues to preach about  human rights press freedom democracy but  when it comes to its america it's  palestinian-american citizen then then  there's an exception  yes the road is difficult it's tough but  we will not be discouraged  shireen stood for truth she stood for  justice and she would have done the same  if it was anyone else so we will  continue our fight for accountability  and we will continue to publicly speak  out  uh and call on secretary lincoln and the  biden administration to follow through  with meaningful action  and to investigate  uh this this crime  there are murals uh around the  palestinian territories we've got her  reports which we which we watch and look  back on ways to remember her legacy for  you and for your family how do you do  that how do you remember her  we remember shirina every day ever she's  part of our lives you know we continue  to talk about her we continue to  remember her and recite our  stories and memories with chilean i  continue to talk with her friends on  daily basis and share stories with them  and share memories  you know it's been 100 days but every  single day we still talk about chilean  everyone still talks about shireen  shireen continues to be everywhere  and  talking about her  and honoring her legacy  means honoring her exceptional and  everlasting legacy so we will continue  our  our efforts towards making sure that her  legacy is everlasting absolutely i'm i'm  very sorry for your loss lena thank you  for joining us  thank you for having me thank you and we  here at al jazeera also continue to  demand full accountability for shireen's  murder

